// HSTIA //

!! The high speed TIA is disabled by default and is turned on by setting AFECON [11] = 1
* Inputs: The SE0, AIN0, AIN1, AIN2, and AIN3/BUF_VREF1V8 input pins.► The DE0 input pin, which has its own RLOAD/RTIA
* The gain resistor (RTIA) options are 50 Ω to 160 kΩ for the DE0 input, and 200 Ω to 160 kΩ for all other input pins

HSRTIACON -> High Speed RTIA Configuration Register
  .CTIACON:   Configure capacitor in parallel with RTIA. This capacitor stabilizes the amplifier loop. When this bit is set, the capacitor is added in parallel with the RTIA resistor.
  .TIASW6CON: SW6 switch control. Use the SW6 switch to select whether or not to use the diode in parallel with RTIA
  .RTIACON:   Configure general RTIA value. To use this RTIA resistor, close the T9 switch (SWCON, Bit 17) and open the T10 switch (SWCON, Bit 17).

DE0RESCON -> DE0 High Speed TIA Resistors Configuration Register
  .DE0RCON: RLOAD_DE0 and RTIA_DE0 setting. To use this RLOAD_DE0 and RTIA_DE0 setting, open the T9 switch, close the T10 switch, and set the RTIA resistor values (see Table 36).

HSTIACON -> High Speed TIA Configuration Register
  .VBIASSEL: Select high speed TIA positive input.

