// PROGRAMMABLE SWITCH MATRIX //

!! Two options are available for controlling the switches on the switch matrix
  ► Control the Tx/TR1, Nx/Nxx, Px/Pxx, and Dx/DR0 switches as a group in the SWCON register
  ► Individual control of each switch within the switch matrix using the xSWFULLCON registers

SWCON -> This register allows configuration of the switch matrix
  .T10CON:      Control of the T10 switch
  .T9CON:       Control of the T9 switch
  .SWSOURCESEL: Switch control select. This bit selects the registers to control the programmable switches
  .TMUXCON:     Control of the Tx/TR1 switch mux. Does not include control of the T9 or T10 switch
  .NMUXCON:     Control of N switch mux
  .PMUXCON:     Control of Px/Pxx switch mux
  .DMUXCON:     Control of Dx/DR0 switch mux

Control reg. switches
  DSWFULLCON -> The DSWFULLCON register allows individual control of the Dx/DR0 switches
  NSWFULLCON -> The NSWFULLCON register allows individual control of the Nx/Nxx switches
  PSWFULLCON -> The PSWFULLCON register allows individual control of the Px/Pxx switches
  TSWFULLCON -> The TSWFULLCON register allows individual control of the Tx/TR1 switches

Read reg. switches
  DSWSTA -> The DSWSTA register indicates the status of the Dx/DR0 switches
  PSWSTA -> The PSWSTA register indicates the status of the Px/Pxx switches
  NSWSTA -> The NSWSTA register indicates the status of the Nx/Nxx switches
  TSWSTA -> The TSWSTA register indicates the status of the Tx/TR1 switches

