// WAVEFORM GENERATOR //

!! To enable the waveform generator block, set the WAVEGENEN bit in the AFECON register to 1, until either the block is disabled (WAVEGENEN = 0) or another source is selected

WGCON -> Waveform generator configuration register
  .DACGAINCAL:   Bypass DAC gain. Use the DAC gain calculated during the Analog Devices factory trim and stored in the DACGAIN register
  .DACOFFSETCAL: Bypass DAC Offset. Use the DAC offset calculated during the calibration routine
  .TYPESEL:      These bits select the type of waveform

SEQCNT -> The SEQCNT register forms the command count, which is incremented by 1 each time the sequencer executes a command. This register is not key protected
  .Count: Sequencer command count. This count is incremented by 1 each time the sequencer executes a command. Reset to 0 by writing 1 to this register. 
        Write 1 to this register also to clear the SEQCRC register.

WGFCW -> Waveform generator register, sinusoid frequency control word.

 WGPHASE -> Waveform generator register, sinusoid phase offset
  !! This register must be set before setting the TYPESEL bit in the WGCON register and the WAVEGENEN bit in the AFECON register

WGOFFSET -> Waveform generator register, sinusoid offset
  !! This register must be set before setting the TYPESEL bit in the WGCON register and the WAVEGENEN bit in the AFECON register.

SINEOFFSET -> Waveform generator register, sinusoid amplitude
  !! This register must be set before setting the TYPESEL bit in the WGCON register and the WAVEGENEN bit in the AFECONvregister.
  ! The DAC output voltage is determined by this value, as well as the ATTENEN bit and the INAMPGNMDE bit in the HSDACCON register.

